# Appendix C — Tracking & Measurement Upgrade Specification

## 1. Purpose and current baseline

This specification upgrades the existing measurement stack; it does not rebuild it from zero.

| Existing asset | Verified state | Treatment |
|---|---|---|
| Google Ads account | **9258098368** | Retain; isolate Consulting conversion goals from Physiotherapy |
| Consulting Search campaign | **700072710** | Retain and repair its bidding inputs |
| Bidding strategy | **Maximize Conversions**, no target CPA; standard strategy, not portfolio | Retain initially while conversion actions are cleaned; do not introduce tCPA until sufficient clean volume exists |
| GA4 property | **316175981** | Retain existing link; create or verify a Consulting-only web data stream |
| Auto-tagging | **On** | Retain; preserve GCLID, GBRAID and WBRAID through the landing page and CRM |
| Current reporting | Last 30d: **A$4,246 spend, 26 reported conversions** | Do not use the 26 as a clean lead baseline |
| Current lead estimate | Last 30d: approximately **20 real leads**, approximately **A$212 per lead** | Treat as a provisional raw-lead baseline, not qualified-lead performance |
| Commercial scale | Approximately **A$40k trailing 12mo**; observed range **A$3.0k–A$4.7k per month** | Measurement must support optimisation of the mature Search programme and the addition of Meta TOFU |
| Meta | No paid-social activity in the verified last-90d GA4 evidence | Implement a dedicated ErgoWorks Consulting Pixel/Dataset and CAPI pipeline before spend |

The shared Google Ads account also contains Physiotherapy activity. ErgoWorks Consulting measurement must be isolated from Physiotherapy, ErgoEquip and Biosymm through campaign-specific conversion goals, separate platform datasets, a Consulting-only GA4 stream, and tightly scoped GTM triggers.

No live account changes are authorised by this plan.

## 2. Conversion-action repair

The current last-30d total of 26 conversions comprises 10 `Calls from ads`, 10 `Make an Enquiry`, 4 `Newsletter Sign Up`, 1 `Email Click` and 1 `Call Forwarding`. Newsletter is currently counted as Primary, while no offline qualified-lead import exists.

### Proposed Google Ads conversion treatment

| Action | Google treatment | Count setting | Reason |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Valid Snapshot request | Primary initially | One | Genuine B2B lead request |
| Direct enquiry form | Primary initially | One | Genuine B2B lead request |
| Qualified call | Primary only via the qualified import once reliable | One | Requires the client-approved qualification rule below; raw/native calls remain Secondary |
| Qualified lead | Secondary during validation; Primary after sufficient clean offline volume | One | Preferred future bidding signal |
| Proposal sent | Secondary | One | Pipeline diagnostic and value calibration |
| Closed won | Secondary initially; value-bearing optimisation input only after sufficient volume | One | Revenue outcome and CAC source of truth |
| Newsletter signup | Secondary | One | Nurture action, not a sales lead |
| Email click | Secondary | One | Soft interaction; not evidence of contact |
| Raw click-to-call / Call Forwarding | Secondary | One | A click or connection alone does not establish lead quality |
| Raw `Calls from ads` | Secondary until qualification is available | One | Current action does not prove valid business intent |
| Page views, engaged visits, downloads, form starts | Secondary / observation only | One | Audience and funnel diagnostics only |
| Physiotherapy or `sydneyphysiotherapist.com.au` actions | Excluded from Consulting campaign goals | — | Prevents cross-business bidding contamination |
| ErgoEquip or Biosymm actions | Never attached to Consulting goals or tags | — | Separate businesses and datasets |

Use Google Ads native conversion actions as the bidding source where technically appropriate. Keep equivalent GA4 key events for analysis and observation only. Do not count both a GA4-imported event and a native Google Ads action for the same conversion.

### Qualified-call definition and W-Audit hook

The final rule must be identical to the definition adopted in Appendix E/W-Audit. Until that rule is approved, use this proposed implementation hook:

> **Awaiting client approval:** a qualified call is a unique inbound call attributable to ErgoWorks Consulting that reaches a human or approved call-handling service, meets the approved minimum connected-duration and operating-hours conditions, and is dispositioned as a legitimate B2B workplace-ergonomics enquiry. It must exclude spam, wrong numbers, job seekers, suppliers, consumer equipment-shopping enquiries, Physiotherapy, clinical or personal-health enquiries, and repeat calls about the same opportunity.

Duration is a screening condition, not proof of qualification. The CRM/call-tracking disposition is authoritative. The exact duration and operating-hours rule remains **awaiting client approval**. Keep any native duration-based proxy **Secondary**. Import `qualified_call` as the only Primary call signal using a stable order ID derived from the CRM opportunity/call record. If a proxy was previously imported in error, retract or restate it with Google Ads conversion adjustments before the qualified import; never count the proxy and qualified import as two conversions for the same call.

## 3. Canonical funnel and bidding map

The following is the single canonical funnel. Snapshot requests, direct enquiries and calls are alternative lead-entry paths; each then progresses through the same CRM stages.

```text
Paid or organic visit
        │
        ├── Snapshot request ──┐
        ├── Direct enquiry ────┼──> Lead record ──> Qualified lead ──> Proposal ──> Won
        └── Call ──────────────┘
              │
              └── Qualified call when W-Audit rule is satisfied
```

The **free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot is preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.** This caveat must appear beside every Snapshot form, ad description and confirmation flow.

| Funnel stage | Canonical event | Source of truth | Google bidding treatment | Meta bidding treatment |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Snapshot request | `snapshot_request` | CRM-confirmed form submission | Initial Primary | Initial website `Lead` optimisation event |
| Direct enquiry | `direct_enquiry` | CRM-confirmed form submission | Initial Primary | Initial website `Lead` optimisation event |
| Call connected | `call_connected` | Call-tracking platform | Secondary | Reporting only |
| Qualified call | `qualified_call` | CRM/call disposition applying W-Audit rule | Primary only via qualified import once reliable | Send through CAPI; optimisation only after reliable volume |
| Qualified lead | `lead_qualified` | CRM stage | Secondary while validated; future Primary | Future `QualifiedLead`/conversion-leads optimisation signal |
| Proposal | `proposal_sent` | CRM stage | Secondary | CAPI reporting/custom audience |
| Won | `closed_won` | CRM finance-approved stage | Value-bearing secondary initially | CAPI value event and audience exclusion |

### Bidding transition rule

**Initially**

- Google campaign 700072710 continues with Maximize Conversions and no tCPA, bidding only to cleaned Snapshot requests, direct enquiries and qualified calls.
- Initially, Meta optimises to website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only.
- Newsletter, email clicks, raw call clicks and other soft events remain observable but cannot influence bidding.

Snapshot booked and held are CRM stages only, not platform events.

**After sufficient offline volume**

- Move Google’s campaign-specific goal toward `lead_qualified` only after the event is deduplicated, timely, consistently defined and producing at least **30 clean qualified conversions per month** for a stable evaluation period. Until then, tCPA/tROAS remains premature.
- Move Meta toward CRM-qualified-lead optimisation only after the event is arriving reliably, match quality is acceptable, and volume is sufficient for stable delivery. Do not force a fixed threshold before Meta’s actual learning diagnostics and the qualified-lead baseline are known.
- Use `closed_won` for value calibration, CAC reporting and eventual value-based optimisation only when deal volume, contribution value and upload consistency are adequate.

These are transition gates, not automatic scale instructions.

## 4. Target architecture

```text
ErgoWorks Consulting landing page and website
        │
        ├── CMP establishes consent before measurement tags
        │
        ├── Web GTM, Consulting-scoped triggers
        │       ├── Conversion Linker
        │       ├── GA4 client forwarding
        │       ├── Google Ads conversion events
        │       └── Meta Pixel events
        │
        └── tags.ergoworksconsulting.com.au
                ├── Server-side GTM privacy filters
                ├── GA4 property 316175981 / Consulting stream
                ├── Google Ads Enhanced Conversions
                └── Meta CAPI, preferably CAPI Gateway

Forms, calls and calendar
        │
        └── CRM lead record
                ├── click IDs, event IDs and consent evidence
                ├── qualification and pipeline stages
                └── Google Data Manager + Meta CAPI offline uploads
```

### Required isolation

- Use a dedicated ErgoWorks Consulting Meta Pixel/Dataset; never reuse ErgoEquip or Biosymm datasets.
- Use a dedicated Consulting GA4 web stream where practicable. If the current property must remain shared, enforce hostname/data-stream filters and reporting boundaries.
- Use a separate web GTM container or explicit allowlisted hostname/path triggers.
- Configure server-container clients and tags to reject non-ErgoWorks hostnames.
- Apply Google campaign-specific conversion goals to campaign 700072710 rather than account-default goals that include Physiotherapy.
- Do not use account-wide conversion-goal changes that could alter Physiotherapy bidding.
- Test that `sydneyphysiotherapist.com.au`, ErgoEquip and Biosymm events cannot enter the Consulting dataset, CRM pipeline or platform uploads.

## 5. Event and parameter specification

Canonical names must remain identical between browser, server and CRM implementations. Add `schema_version` to every custom event and increment it when definitions change.

| Event | Trigger and canonical meaning | Permitted business parameters | Destinations | Bidding status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `view_service` | Consulting service page viewed after consent | `service_type`, `page_path_clean`, `cx_funnel_step`, `schema_version` | GA4; consented audiences | Secondary |
| `form_start` | User begins an approved Consulting form | `form_name`, `offer_type`, `service_type`, `event_id`, `schema_version` | GA4, Meta | Secondary |
