## 13. KPI and reconciliation framework

The primary commercial optimisation KPI is **cost per qualified lead**, not reported platform conversions or raw form CPL.

| KPI | Formula | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Raw CPL | Media spend ÷ valid Snapshot requests, direct enquiries and connected lead calls | Entry-stage efficiency |
| Cost per qualified lead | Media spend ÷ unique CRM-qualified leads | Primary channel KPI |
| Qualified-lead rate | Qualified leads ÷ valid raw leads | Lead-quality diagnostic |
| Cost per proposal | Media spend ÷ proposals sent | Pipeline efficiency |
| CAC | Total attributable acquisition cost ÷ closed-won customers | Commercial efficiency |
| Media-only CAC | Media spend ÷ closed-won customers | Channel comparison; label clearly |
| Lead-to-won rate | Closed-won customers ÷ valid raw leads | Funnel calibration |
| Qualified-lead-to-won rate | Closed-won customers ÷ qualified leads | Target-CPL calibration |
| Target qualified CPL | Target CAC × qualified-lead-to-won rate | Maximum affordable qualified-lead cost |
| Target raw CPL | Target qualified CPL × qualified-lead rate | Maximum affordable raw-lead cost |
| Pipeline value per qualified lead | Expected contribution profit × qualified-lead-to-won probability | Offline conversion value |
| Platform-to-CRM discrepancy | Absolute platform conversions minus matched CRM conversions, divided by CRM conversions | Tracking diagnostic |
| Missing-click-ID rate | Leads without eligible click ID ÷ attributable paid leads | Offline-match diagnostic |
| Duplicate-lead rate | Duplicate lead records ÷ total lead records | CRM integrity |
| Upload success rate | Accepted offline events ÷ eligible events | Pipeline health |

“Total attributable acquisition cost” should include media, agency/consulting fees, creative, landing-page costs and other agreed acquisition costs. Contribution profit, not headline revenue, should be used for target-CAC decisions where available.

No target CAC, target qualified CPL or scale threshold should be committed until average contract value, contribution margin, qualification rate and close rate are verified.

### First 90-day measurement commitments

Commit only to measurable leading indicators:

- 100% of approved Primary actions documented and tested
- Newsletter and soft actions removed from Consulting bidding goals
- Physiotherapy actions excluded from campaign 700072710 goals
- CRM lead IDs and event IDs present on valid lead records
- Offline uploads operating within the latency thresholds
- Meta lead-event EMQ at least 8.0
- Browser/server deduplication at least 90%
- Server/client hit ratio between 80% and 120%
- At least six applicable Meta match parameters on eligible lead events
- Platform-to-CRM reconciliation reported weekly
- Zero sensitive-data events or parameters detected in launch testing

These are implementation and data-quality commitments, not promised reductions in CPL, claims or injury outcomes.

