   359	## 11. Attribution configuration
   360	
   361	- Use **Data-Driven Attribution (DDA)** for eligible Google Ads conversion actions and GA4 reporting.
   362	- Do not use first-click, linear, position-based, time-decay or other rule-based attribution.
   363	- Use a provisional **30-day Google click window** for B2B lead generation, then review actual conversion lag quarterly. Extend toward 60–90 days only if CRM evidence shows the sales cycle requires it.
   364	- Treat Meta’s platform attribution using its supported settings; begin with the standard 7-day click/1-day view reporting context where required, but treat view-through conversions as directional rather than proof of incrementality.
   365	- Use CRM-qualified and closed-won records as the commercial source of truth across platforms.
   366	- Report platform-attributed, GA4-attributed and CRM-sourced outcomes separately; do not force them to reconcile as if they use identical windows and models.
